.. raw:: html

    <div class="sphx-glr-thumbcontainer" tooltip="Michael Herman and Edward Kluk&#x27;s 1984 method propagates a quantum wavepacket by summing many classical trajectories rather than following just one: launch one fixed-width (&quot;frozen&quot;) Gaussian wavepacket from every point of a phase-space grid under the initial state, propagate each one along its own classical trajectory, and sum the results with a monodromy-built prefactor and classical action phase,">

.. only:: html

  .. image:: /api/gallery/semiclassical/propagators/images/thumb/sphx_glr_plot_herman_kluk_wavepacket_thumb.png
